        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4c445c49-751a-5030-995d-0a679da55db9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Mercer\n- Organizations: Kansas City Chiefs\n- Events: 1966 AFL Championship, first AFL-NFL World Championship Game, Super Bowl I\n- Places: Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum, Los Angeles, California\n- Topics: professional American football\n\nFacts:\n- Mike Mercer was a member of the Kansas City Chiefs team that won the 1966 AFL Championship.\n- The Kansas City Chiefs' 1966 AFL Championship team played in the first AFL-NFL World Championship Game.\n- The first AFL-NFL World Championship Game in professional American football was played on January 15, 1967.\n- The first AFL-NFL World Championship Game was later called Super Bowl I.\n- Some contemporaneous reports, including the game's radio broadcast, referred to the first AFL-NFL World Championship Game as the Super Bowl.\n- Super Bowl I was played at the Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum in Los Angeles, California.",
